integ5 0067 = patches/attn5/0067-glm-dsa-decode-select-many-ctas.patch (overnight 2026-10-31), renumbered for the integrated stack on 3f94715d.

attn5 0067 (T5(a), overnight 2026-10-31): a decode window's DSA select on many CTAs, exact.

Replaces tf_glm_select_rows_wide (one 1,024-thread CTA a row: four radix scans plus an emit scan of the row) for decode
windows (rows <= Scratch.bits_rows, np >= 4096) with two launches (zig/kernels/cuda/glm_index_decode.cuh, in glm_glue.cu):
  tf_glm_dsel_scan  grid (cdiv(last row's pools, 4096), rows), 256 threads: every CTA of a row computes the same floor (the
                    need-th best of glm_index_pools' 4,096 sampled order keys, 4 warp-aggregated radix passes) and writes
                    its span's "above the floor" and "at the floor" ballot words (2 bits a pool, no zeroing needed);
  tf_glm_dsel_merge a 1,024-thread CTA a row: popcounts and block scans of the words, then
                    ties path   (n_gt < K <= n_ge: the floor is the K-th key) every gt pool + the first K - n_gt eq pools;
                    candidates  (<= 4,096, pool order, in shared memory) tf_glm_select_rows' radix select;
                    otherwise   today's full-row select (1,024 threads); rows of <= 4,096 pools are selected whole.
Every path returns tf_glm_select_rows' bytes: the K best sparse._order_key(fp32 score) values over [0, max(vis, K))
clipped to np, ties to the lower pool, ascending. TF_GLM_DSEL=0 keeps today's select (unset or 1: on; a typo is refused).
Scratch: Scratch.ls on decode buffers grows to bitsBytes(min(seg, 48), capacity / 4) (~0.8 MiB a decode buffer set at
864K); prefill buffers keep bits_rows 0 (prompt tails keep tf_glm_select_rows_wide).
Checks: zig build test-glm-index-host (launch rules), test-glm-index-emulate (host C++ model, all four paths),
tf-cuda-test glm-index-check (GPU: planted kinds at 7 windows up to 864K x 16 rows against tf_glm_select_rows, all
four paths required; then selectTokens with and without the decode select: scores, pools, token lists, counts equal).

